#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:53
#: eff128dbed604fb48b5ecd35839c6cbd
msgid "There have been many versions of this board and many clones. Best results, with no feature/performance impacts will be obtained boards which have solder jumpers for selecting \"SBUS\" or \"PPM\" RX input. This should be soldered to the \"PPM\" selection for ALL receiver types. ArduPilot will automatically detect and accept any supported format (SBUS/PPM/DSM/etc.) on the RX input with this jumper selection. In addition, be sure the board has a barometer, SD Card slot, and Current sense circuit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:56
#: 322053edb40346d3b3440993c1ea2aa4
msgid "Board Connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:57
#: b413ed09b47449479a0ade19f15981c8
msgid "GPS is attached to UART6 (SERIAL3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:59
#: 5f3bc4e8987048e2a09ebdfa9722bed8
msgid "Telem is available at UART 1 (SERIAL1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:61
#: cb14118dee5f43cfb11b0fd4bda1cfe0
msgid "The shared USART3/I2C pins are ,by default, enabled only for I2C operation to allow external compass or digital airspeed sensor attachment.If at least one device attached externally, does not have pull-up resistors, then 2K ohm pull-up resistors will need to be added externally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:63
#: 8997b79f6e8541a08625843a0556e88c
msgid "However, by setting :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` to 1, the external I2C connection is disabled, so that USART3 may be used as a normal UART. It is SERIAL2 in the parameters listings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:65
#: 1ed7e97747ad4ead90a0d7bb232c92f2
msgid "The board's RSSI pad can be used as an analog RSSI input. Use pin \"0\" as the RSSI input pin in Mission Planner. Mission planner default values for battery voltage and current scales are provided, however since many variations of this board are available, these may needed to be manually calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:67
#: 1e60dd4ab18a490a9be1fff8fd097f99
msgid "The RSSI pad can be re-purposed to be the TX output of UART4 instead of analog RSSI input, if the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` param is set to 2 or 3. And if :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` param is set to 3, then PWM output pin 5 becomes instead, the RX pin of UART4 to provide a full addition UART. Also, if :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` param is set to 4, then both UART3 and UART4 are active and available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:69
#: 785bdb38b16c44e9bbe5beb36c3de721
msgid "If you want to power the servos from the ESC BEC via the board's center rail for the servo outputs, then you should remove the diode as per here: https://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?2874687, otherwise, independently power the servos directly from the ESC or independent BEC with no connection to the board's servo output center rail. The VCC pin next to the RX in pin is a 5V output only and not affected by this modification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:75
#: 76e1d3f65feb4ba184443410794ae56f
msgid "Video power provided on the video input and output center rail, is provide through an on-board noise filter. Either ~4.5V (labeled 5V) or VBAT-0.5V (VBAT) can be selected by solder pads on the back of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:77
#: fbad2e597fec4a7daaac7f5d7c1f26a5
msgid "PPM solder pad/resistor should be soldered and “S-BUS” resistor/solder pad removed Otherwise, UART1 or UART6 or RCIN will not work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:85
#: 732d0fa7d538451d86597bac4df66e9f
msgid "PWM Outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:87
#: feed947b7a2f461b9e1c0c578411371b
msgid "The Pro version has 6 PWM outputs available on thru-hole pads, and two additional (PWM7 & PWM8) on the rear, via solder pads above the \"MOTO\" silk screen printing. The AIO version only provides 6 PWM outputs via thru-hole pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:94
#: 501e7487fbf4479abb0ec15ba331a99d
msgid "Default UART order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:96
#: eee400dde2f44ce89db52d509b7c1731
msgid "SERIAL0 = console = USB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:97
#: 841c638e3024477c9ed2126378146dd4
msgid "SERIAL1 = Telemetry1 = USART1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:98
#: 0945e8f37875475db52ee629038319f4
msgid "SERIAL2 = not assigned (Telemetry2 = USART3 if :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` =1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:99
#: 1a268c5d55d14e3397b36ff0b06712eb
msgid "SERIAL3 = GPS1 = USART6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:100
#: 6df9c37ebe564760883fb52ba74f0383
msgid "SERIAL4 = GPS2 = UART4 (if :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` = 2 or 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:101
#: 4588b5406d414c59bfea375f824395fe
msgid "SERIAL5 = not assigned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:102
#: c8ab755dae464be589210c10c0cad62c
msgid "SERIAL6 = not assigned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:104
#: 64769259979e47a98961a9039469de6a
msgid "Serial protocols can be adjusted to personal preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:107
#: d5a5f35cd7124e9b82942114ec3277be
msgid "Dshot capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:109
#: 7dccac3e39d84f60b66e24a66eec831a
msgid "All motor/servo outputs are Dshot and PWM capable. However, mixing Dshot and normal PWM operation for outputs is restricted into groups, ie. enabling Dshot for an output in a group requires that ALL outputs in that group be configured and used as Dshot, rather than PWM outputs. The output groups that must be the same (PWM rate or Dshot, when configured as a normal servo/motor output) are: 1/2/6, 3/4/5, 7/8(Pro only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:112
#: a995949d07f847e88fb3a0bd74209bcf
msgid "Flashing Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:113
#: 271b63ab9487430e833f91adeb2b04fc
msgid "Usually these boards are sold pre-flashed with betaflight / INav firwares and require both firmware and bootloader to be updated if you want to use ArduPilot, as an ArduPilot-compatible bootloader is required for subsequent ArduPilot firmware-upgrade handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:115
#: 85915223410046ba87fe5b53dab9c9df
msgid "Firmware files can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__. Use omnibusf4pro firmware for the OmnibusF4Pro boards and omnibusf4 firmware for the AIO versions. The pro version will be used in the following examples. Besides the .apj files for firmware flashing via MissionPlanner, there's also .hex files for use with various utilities like dfu-util or betaflight / iNav GUIs. You will also find a _bl.hex that contains the firmware plus the ArduPilot compatible bootloader in case it is not already present on your board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:119
#: 12f19cf207c84bf1a9af8aa59f134632
msgid "The provided _bl.hex file can be flashed using BF or iNav GUI, likely the most convenient way to get ArduPilot on your board the first time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:121
#: 1c5b80a2c3e74c73b745e2b38ce7abab
msgid "Alternatively, the bootloader can be flashed separately. This requires the board to be put into DFU mode. Tools like dfu-util can be used to flash the bootlader. Once the bootlader is present, all subsequent firmware updates can be done using MissionPlanner's firmware functions."
msgstr ""

